  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, which builds the spider and animates it. It typechecks. I couldn't run it in a browser here, so I haven't seen a rendered frame and the camera framing, shadows and backdrop look are untested.\n\nThe scene uses the `product-studio` look preset for backdrop, light and shadows. A large light-grey plane is the ground. The camera is a fixed three-quarter perspective aimed at the spider, with no user input.\n\nThe spider is only primitives:\n- **Body:** abdomen and thorax with an orange abdomen mark, plus a head, four eye spheres and two cone fangs.\n- **Legs:** eight legs, each a femur and tibia joined by a knee, with a ball at the hip and the foot.\n\nThe gait runs on a 2-second loop:\n- **Diagonals:** legs on opposite diagonals step together, half a cycle apart.\n- **Swing and plant:** in its half of the cycle each foot lifts, swings forward and plants. During the other half it stays planted while the body moves over it.\n- **Foot placement:** each foot's path is turned into joint angles each frame, so planted feet should stay on the ground. This is untested.\n- **Bob:** the body bobs twice per cycle, once per diagonal step.\n\n`window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` plus two animation frames, which should be after the first frame has been drawn.",
